    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d448">

                <pb facs="1079" n="1045" xml:id="pg1045"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.60/8–1947: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Embassy in the United Kingdom
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-08-21T19:00:00-04:00">August 21, 1947—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3609. Identic notes from Benelux countries of nature described paragraph 7 urtel 4500, Aug 19,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d448-f1"
                    /> received here yesterday. It is our intention to inform the Paris Conference
                    of any revised level of industry plan as soon as it has been decided by the US
                    and UK Govts and simultaneously with its announcement. We can further agree that
                    US–UK could individually keep these interested Govts informed during the London
                    talks, but this should be a US–UK not a tripartite decision. Should these Govts
                    wish to present written comments it must be understood that in receiving these
                    views we cannot agree thereby to any delay in the announcement September first
                    of the level of industry plan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
